{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794471094,"nonce":"v6carOWmfiajTyYzBWyZXsNJS6o=","message":"Priority note, 2026-11-12: the browser is the target and wasmtime is the test harness, so the two wasmtime-only fiber gaps (loopSum, cold compile of the unit suite) are not blockers. V8 has no fiber gap left.\n\nWould \"save only the live locals in the unwind exit\" also help the browser? It shrinks the module a little, not much. Unit suite, direct, Mac: 12.36 MB plain -\u003e 20.90 MB with fibers (+8.5 MB; LLVM 20.50 -\u003e 28.31). The module has 75,149 locals and 188,276 call sites. At roughly 16 bytes per saved local (prologue load + exit store) the save/restore code is about 1.2 MB of that growth, under 6% of the module. The per-call-site epilogue (state test, ordinal store, branch, about 15 bytes) is about 2.9 MB at most, so it is the larger part, and it is what to cut if module size matters. These byte counts are estimates from instruction sizes, not measured per section.\n\nSo live-locals is a wasmtime compile-time fix (register pressure), not a download-size fix. Not started; the correctness risk is a silent wrong resume, which only the threads suite would catch.","files":null}]}